[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3982048388","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116943#issuecomment-3982048388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116943","id":3982048388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tWTyE","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T04:48:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T04:48:41Z","body":"* See also #111397.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3982048388/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3984408200","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116943#issuecomment-3984408200","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116943","id":3984408200,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tfT6I","user":{"login":"zimonitrome","id":17656709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjU2NzA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17656709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome","html_url":"https://github.com/zimonitrome","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T13:29:58Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T13:29:58Z","body":"Note: This PR does *not* implement function type inference.\r\n\r\nThing like this:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n#                ↓ note: no explicit return type\r\nfunc a(x: int):\r\n    return float(x) / 2.0\r\nvar b := a(5)\r\n```\r\nwill still not work.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, thing like this will still not work:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\ndef a(k: int) -> int:\r\n    if k > 5:\r\n        return null\r\n    else:\r\n        return k\r\n\r\nvar b := [2,5,10].map(a).filter(func(x): return x != null)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlthough this last example could be possible if we add a check in `array.filter` to check if all items have the same type. Might be a bit too much for this PR? But it would be nice... (currently not in the PR)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhat this PR does do is:\r\n\r\n- `Array.filter()` preserves the source typed element type (`Array[T] -> Array[T]`).\r\n- `Array.map()` infers `Array[R]` only when the callable’s return type is explicitly declared and non-`Variant` i.e.:\r\n  ```gdscript\r\n  #                  ↓ this part here\r\n  func a(x: int) -> float:\r\n      return float(x) / 2.0\r\n  ```\r\n  since this already works:\r\n  ```gdscript\r\n  func a(x: int) -> float:\r\n      return float(x) / 2.0\r\n  var b := a(5)\r\n  ```\r\n\r\nIf the callable return type is omitted (or is `Variant`), `map()` stays untyped (`Array`).","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3984408200/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4022369614","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116943#issuecomment-4022369614","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116943","id":4022369614,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vwH1O","user":{"login":"zimonitrome","id":17656709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjU2NzA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17656709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome","html_url":"https://github.com/zimonitrome","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T09:30:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T09:30:06Z","body":"If the `map()` implementation is too verbose/awkward, perhaps splitting it up into two different PRs would be better suited?\r\n\r\nThe `filter()` implementation of just copying the previous type is a no-brainer (and much cleaner) IMO.\r\n\r\nAny thoughts?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4022369614/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4032007092","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116943#issuecomment-4032007092","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116943","id":4032007092,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wU4u0","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T14:48:57Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T14:48:57Z","body":"Thanks for the PR! In my opinion, as I stated in #111397, we shouldn't add special cases and hardcode type info on the GDScript side, since the core doesn't provide the corresponding information about generic methods.","au